# Keep this repo LF end to end, in the index and in the working tree.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the development machine here, which normalizes on
# commit but writes CRLF back out on checkout — that is how the sibling
# Utility Suite repo ended up a per-file mix of CRLF and LF, and why editing a
# file there means sniffing its line endings first. Pinning `eol=lf` means a
# fresh clone matches what is committed and nothing has to be sniffed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched by the normalizer.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.webm binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
